# Warframe Market Stocks

Personal platinum flip / price-drop monitor. Free-tier only.

## Stack
- Next.js 15 App Router + TypeScript + Tailwind (`src/`)
- Supabase Postgres (no Redis/Upstash)
- Deploy: Vercel Hobby + GitHub Actions cron (every 3–4h), not Vercel `*/30` cron

## Hard constraints
- WFM API ≤ 3 req/s; descriptive `User-Agent` (`WFM_USER_AGENT`); send `Platform: pc`
- Items + orders: **API v2**; statistics: **API v1** (no v2 equivalent yet)
- Serverless: small batches + `scan_cursor` + self-chain; do not hold one long scan
- Store latest snapshot + ≤7d history; prune aggressively (500 MB DB)
- Cron protected by `CRON_SECRET`; no multi-user auth in MVP
- No marketplace UI clone, no auto-trading, no paid add-ons

## Data (Supabase)
`items`, `scan_cursor`, `item_snapshots`, `item_snapshot_history`, `alerts`, `watchlist`

## Algorithms
- Spread/ROI: visible in-game sells; cheapest vs next listing; ROI = spread / lowest sell; defaults spread ≥ 5p, ROI ≥ 15%
- Price drop: `lowest_sell < median_48h * 0.85`; 24h alert dedupe
- Stats only when needed for price-drop (or every Nth full cycle)

## Scan / watchlist
- `watchlist` may list `url_name`s before they exist in `items`; cron must only snapshot names present in `items` (skip orphans until manifest sync).
- Keep scan single-threaded per invocation (in-process WFM rate limiter is not global across lambdas).

## Orchestration
Large work uses `plan-orchestrator`. Prefer phases: foundation → scanner → dashboard → Discord later.
